clustering (§5) — two readings had to be settled
  1. Rule 1 says "the row joins the cluster of stem(seed)". Read literally, the row
     is keyed on the seed's stem; the row's own stem is NOT fused with the seed's.
     Fusing them chains Variant -> seed -> Variant across the whole feed and
     collapsed 11560 rows into one cluster of 7,661 in a first pass. The
     literal reading is used.
  2. Rule 3's near-miss merge is applied once and never chained. Chaining a prefix
     relation walks k1 -> k11 -> k111 and merges unrelated brands even though no
     non-adjacent pair clears 0.90, which is what the floor exists to prevent.
  The rule-3 floor is taken as binding over the worked example beside it:
  jaro_winkler(dafabet, dafawining) = 0.79, so that pair does not merge.
  result: 1818 clusters, 973 with 2 or more
  URLs, 845 singletons, 55 clusters cover half
